NAME
    manual - discover and present RumiAI operational manual topics

SYNOPSIS
    manual
    manual [--no-pager] <topic>
    manual [--no-pager] <owner> <topic>

DESCRIPTION
    manual accesses revision-coupled operational documentation distributed with
    the current RumiAI OS product revision.

    With no operands, manual discovers all materialized global manual topics and
    writes one owner-qualified identity per line:

        <owner> <topic>

    Discovery output is sorted lexically by owner and then topic. Topic identities
    are always owner-qualified in discovery output, even when a topic name is
    globally unique.

    With one topic operand, manual first searches all materialized global owners
    for an exact topic-name match. One exact match is presented; multiple exact
    matches fail as ambiguous while listing the owner-qualified invocations that
    resolve the ambiguity.

    If no exact topic exists, manual searches topic names for the operand as a
    literal substring, equivalent to *<topic>*. When one or more substring matches
    exist, manual writes their owner-qualified identities to standard output,
    sorted lexically by owner and then topic. This result list is discovery output
    and is not sent through the pager. If the substring search is also empty, the
    request fails as not found.

    With owner and topic operands, manual resolves only that exact owner-local
    topic and does not perform substring fallback or fall back to another owner.

OPTIONS
    --no-pager
        Write an exactly selected topic directly to standard output instead of
        invoking the normal pager. This option is valid only when a topic is
        requested. Substring-search result lists are always written directly.

PRESENTATION
    When --no-pager is absent and an exact topic is selected, manual delegates
    presentation to the technical pager command. pager owns terminal detection
    and host-specific viewer selection.

    --no-pager bypasses pager and writes an exactly selected topic directly to
    standard output. Discovery and substring-search result lists never invoke
    pager.

FILES
    res/<owner>/manual/<topic>
        Owner-qualified global operational manual topic.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m manual [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   Success, including a non-empty substring-search result list.
    1   Invalid invocation or invalid owner/topic identifier.
    2   Requested topic not found and no substring matches found.
    3   Exact unqualified topic is ambiguous.
    4   Execution or presentation failure, including pager failure.

EXAMPLES
    Discover all available topics:

        manual

    Present a globally unique exact topic:

        manual state-path

    Search topic names when no exact topic exists:

        manual state

    Resolve an ambiguous exact topic explicitly:

        manual ai pkg
        manual sys pkg

    Write a selected topic directly without paging:

        manual --no-pager sys pkg

SEE ALSO
    pager
